		{"id":"7c9e807835c48c67","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Locations/Eos Multiverse/The Dark Forest Zone/Local Cluster/Totum/Verse Structure/Superclusters/Laniakea/Milky Way Galaxy/Sol System/Earth (Terra)/1890-2078/Pre-WW3/Faction Profile/Neo Xia Sovereignty.md","x":-720,"y":-140,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"ecfaccd4db95e7c5","type":"file","file":"Workshop/Work On/Sort/North Korea.md","x":320,"y":-140,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"b9fba31bcf964e3d","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/I - Pleroma Archive/World/Locations/Eos Multiverse/The Dark Forest Zone/Local Cluster/Totum/Verse Structure/Superclusters/Laniakea/Milky Way Galaxy/Sol System/Earth (Terra)/1890-2078/Economy & Infrastructure/Locations/Countries/India.md","x":-200,"y":360,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"00a8e97369dbd1d7","type":"text","text":"The Systemic Architect\n\nPolitical Structure\n\nOne-party civilizational state\n\nMeritocratic technocracy at the top\n\nHeavy surveillance and data-driven governance\n\nLeader Archetype (2040s)\n\nNot a cult-of-personality ruler\n\nA Chairman-Administrator figure\n\nBackground: systems engineering, economics, logistics\n\nThinks in 50–100 year horizons\n\nInternal Control Method\n\nPredictive governance\n\nSocial credit + resource access\n\nPreemptive suppression, not reactive repression\n\nChina’s role in CRINK:\n\nLong-term planner\n\nIndustrial backbone\n\nAI, infrastructure, and population management\n\nWilling to sacrifice growth for stability\n\nChina is the brain of CRINK.","x":-1240,"y":-154,"width":398,"height":428},
		{"id":"36ac4d42c25c4acf","type":"text","text":"The Demographic Balancer\n\nPolitical Structure\n\nElectoral democracy sliding toward civilizational nationalism\n\nStrong executive, weakened pluralism\n\nBureaucratic inertia everywhere else\n\nLeader Archetype (2040s)\n\nPopulist-nationalist with technocratic advisors\n\nBalances tradition, growth, and resentment\n\nExtremely sensitive to sovereignty and status\n\nInternal Control Method\n\nElectoral legitimacy + cultural identity\n\nRegional autonomy tolerated until it isn’t\n\nHeavy use of internal security forces, not ideology\n\nIndia’s role in CRINK:\n\nPopulation mass\n\nLabor and manufacturing redundancy\n\nStrategic ambiguity (never fully commits)\n\nActs as a counterweight to China inside CRINK\n\nIndia is the counterweight.","x":-200,"y":881,"width":400,"height":399},
		{"id":"8044b7bcc062ae04","type":"text","text":"The Unpredictable Fuse\n\nPolitical Structure\n\nTotalitarian dynastic state\n\nMilitarized society\n\nEconomy structured around survival and leverage\n\nLeader Archetype\n\nHereditary ruler with symbolic authority\n\nReal power diffused among military and security elites\n\nInternal Control Method\n\nTotal information lockdown\n\nRitualized fear\n\nExternal threat mythologized into identity\n\nNorth Korea’s role in CRINK:\n\nNuclear wildcard\n\nPlausible deniability engine\n\nPressure valve for escalation\n\nSacrificial distraction if needed\n\nNorth Korea is the detonator—rarely used, always implied.","x":880,"y":-140,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"41cf994cedbdf61e","type":"text","text":"The Strategic Saboteur\n\nPolitical Structure\n\nNeo-imperial security state\n\nOligarchic remnants subordinated to intelligence services\n\nDeep military–industrial legacy\n\nLeader Archetype (2040s)\n\nFormer intelligence or military command\n\nPragmatic, cynical, historically minded\n\nObsessed with humiliation narratives and restoration\n\nInternal Control Method\n\nControlled chaos\n\nPatronage networks\n\nSelective brutality combined with cultural nationalism\n\nRussia’s role in CRINK:\n\nAsymmetric warfare expertise\n\nDestabilization of Western cohesion\n\nEnergy leverage\n\nWillingness to escalate just short of apocalypse\n\nRussia is the knife.","x":-200,"y":-1240,"width":400,"height":414},
		{"id":"7cdf2a03b431cb5b","type":"text","text":"How CRINK Solves Internal Contradictions\n\nCRINK does not resolve disagreements ideologically. It uses:\n\nCompartmentalization\nConflicts are localized and isolated.\n\nMutual Leverage\nEveryone has dirt on everyone else.\n\nPlausible Conflict\nInternal disputes are allowed if they serve external deception.","x":640,"y":340,"width":371,"height":360},
		{"id":"0bcdf545a8280eac","type":"file","file":"New Readers Start Here/II - Companion Narratives/Syl'Cothan Dominion/1 - Earth/1 - Bipolar World/Proxy wars.md","x":-1000,"y":640,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"083f5fc6b37bc989","type":"text","text":"Prime Minister Arjun Rao\n![[fb25836e-8e31-46d6-bad8-75738140c270.png]]\nPosition: Prime Minister of India\nBackground:\n\t•\tFormer infrastructure minister\n\t•\tRose on anti-corruption and sovereignty rhetoric\n\t•\tSurrounded by technocrats, constrained by coalition politics\n\nPsych Profile:\n\t•\tNationalist but pragmatic\n\t•\tDeeply wary of China\n\t•\tSees India as a civilization delayed, not inferior\n\nView on CRINK:\n\n“We are aligned until alignment costs us our future.”\n\nRole in Evo5/TBS:\n\t•\tOfficially opposed\n\t•\tQuietly allows observation access\n\t•\tIndia never hosts Evo5 labs—but benefits from the distraction\n","x":-496,"y":1360,"width":296,"height":289},
		{"id":"6cc9b24f8d83c389","type":"text","text":"Classification: OBSIDIAN-RED / INTERNAL ONLY\nAuthor: Joint Strategic Viability Committee (JSVC)\n\nSubject: Evo5 / TBS Field Validation — Phase Gamma\n\nThe Indo-Chinese operational theater has successfully masked substrate deployment. Environmental stressors exceeded modeled thresholds, producing both apex and collapse outcomes consistent with Evo5 projections.\n\nTBS-03 (“Urban Breacher Variant”) demonstrated superior mech-counter capability in confined terrain. Control persistence averaged 36–52 hours before behavioral drift rendered assets non-recoverable.\n\nRecommendation:\n\t•\tContinue limited deployment under proxy frameworks\n\t•\tTerminate attempts at long-term control\n\t•\tArchive outcomes, not assets\n\nNote:\nIndian intelligence awareness is assessed at 63%. Tolerable.","x":-1000,"y":1188,"width":402,"height":412},
		{"id":"c985196bf4f59789","type":"text","text":"Classification: JOINT STRATEGIC ASSESSMENT — LEVEL 7\nRecipients: Europolis Council, United American Republics Strategic Command\n\nAssessment:\nWhile the Indo-Chinese conflict appears genuine, inconsistencies suggest coordinated escalation management inconsistent with historical hostility levels.\n\nAnomalous battlefield incidents include:\n\t•\tNon-mechanized assets disabling armored units without conventional anti-tank signatures\n\t•\tInfrared footage of large, fast-moving heat sources inconsistent with known platforms\n\t•\tBiological residue at engagement sites lacking known taxonomic classification\n\nHypothesis:\nCRINK may be testing unconventional counter-mechanized systems under the cover of regional conflict.\n\nRecommendation:\nIncrease ISR allocation. Prepare public deniability.\n\nTone: analytical, uneasy, behind the curve.\n","x":-1480,"y":1188,"width":370,"height":412},
		{"id":"fa9a0552fc446e81","type":"text","text":"Supreme Marshal Kim Yo-jong\n![[7791aead-bf98-4619-83e6-ae26459f24e5.png]]\nPosition: Eternal Leader (symbolic), real power diffused\nRole:\n\t•\tNuclear signaling\n\t•\tEscalation fog\n\t•\tIntelligence noise\n\nEvo5/TBS Role:\n\t•\tNone directly\n\t•\tServes as strategic distraction when needed\n","x":911,"y":-560,"width":338,"height":320},
		{"id":"c2eb3819f8c0ee46","type":"text","text":"President Sergei Volkov\n![[F6E51E12-CF0B-4490-86B8-6A575CF28928.webp]]\nPosition: President of the Russian Federation\nBackground:\n\t•\tFormer GRU strategic planning director\n\t•\tSpecialized in adversarial destabilization and long-horizon sabotage\n\t•\tPersonally involved in post-NATO fracture planning\n\nPsych Profile:\n\t•\tCynical, historically obsessed\n\t•\tBelieves truth is only a temporary condition\n\t•\tSees collapse as inevitable—aims to choose when\n\nView on India-China Conflict:\n\n“A useful wound is better than a clean peace.”\n\nRole in Evo5/TBS:\n\t•\tPushes field deployment\n\t•\tWants operational data, not theory\n\t•\tTreats TBS units as expendable escalation assets\n","x":320,"y":-1195,"width":319,"height":325},
		{"id":"ff9fb51e21db7327","type":"text","text":"Chairman Liu Zhengyuan (刘正元)\n![[168c8313-6099-4eae-b72d-4d7fe4d47d6f.png]]\nPosition: Chairman of the Central Stability Commission\nBackground:\n\t•\tSystems engineer turned macro-economist\n\t•\tFormer architect of China’s national logistics AI\n\t•\tRose through crisis-management portfolios, not party theatrics\n\nPsych Profile:\n\t•\tNot charismatic, not ideological\n\t•\tTreats nations like load-bearing systems\n\t•\tWill sacrifice growth, prestige, even territory if stability curves demand it\n\nView on India:\n\n“India is not an enemy. It is a variable.”\n\nRole in Evo5/TBS:\n\t•\tAuthorizes containment-research, never “weapons”\n\t•\tFrames Evo5/TBS as resilience modeling under contested environments","x":-842,"y":-680,"width":320,"height":295},
		{"id":"2adfe06c61e1ede8","type":"text","text":"Author: Callsign “Gravel-Nine”\nEmployer: Unaffiliated Security Consortium\nLocation: Eastern Ladakh Corridor\n\nI’ve seen drones. Mechs. Experimental junk. This wasn’t that.\n\nIt moved like it knew what the armor would do before it did it. Didn’t charge. Didn’t roar. Just went for joints. Power couplings. Ripped a walker open like it was packaging.\n\nCommand said it was “local fauna.”\nLocal fauna doesn’t stalk patrol routes.\n\nWhatever they’re testing out here, it’s not meant to come home.\n\nWe pulled out. Didn’t get paid.\nNobody chased us","x":-968,"y":1720,"width":370,"height":400},
		{"id":"99482702e4770eda","type":"file","file":"Workshop/Work On/Sort/Telum biologicum suggestum (TBS).md","x":-1495,"y":1720,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"339bf5b5b013a79c","type":"text","text":"(High surveillance, legal warfare, deniable violence)\n\n1. Aegis Continuum\n\nOrigin: Europolis\nPublic Cover: Urban security & infrastructure resilience\nTrue Function: Regime enforcement and internal suppression\n\nSpecialty\n\t•\tRiot control\n\t•\tCounter-insurgency in megacities\n\t•\tData-driven population control\n\nAesthetic\n\t•\tWhite-gray armor, red warning lights\n\t•\tRiot-meets-military\n\t•\tLooks like police who stopped pretending\n\nReputation\n\n“Order without mercy.”\n\n⸻\n\n2. Nordstahl Directive\n\nOrigin: Northern Europe / ex-NATO\nPublic Cover: Defense consulting\nTrue Function: Advanced weapons testing & battlefield analytics\n\nSpecialty\n\t•\tPrototype deployment\n\t•\tAI-assisted targeting trials\n\t•\tRed-team simulation units\n\nAesthetic\n\t•\tMinimalist steel-gray armor\n\t•\tNo insignia\n\t•\tFeels clinical and inhuman\n\nReputation\n\n“You are not fighting them. You are being measured.”\n\n⸻\n\n3. Grey Orchard Group\n\nOrigin: Corporate-state hybrids\nPublic Cover: Critical supply chain security\nTrue Function: Economic warfare enforcement\n\nSpecialty\n\t•\tPort seizures\n\t•\tData sabotage\n\t•\tLabor suppression\n\nAesthetic\n\t•\tBusiness-military fusion\n\t•\tBlack suits over light armor\n\t•\tLooks like executives who carry rifles\n\nReputation\n\n“Markets backed by guns.”\n\n⸻\n\n4. Valence Tactical\n\nOrigin: Franco-Italian alliance\nPublic Cover: Cultural heritage protection\nTrue Function: Counter-revolutionary operations\n\nSpecialty\n\t•\tMuseum cities\n\t•\tHistoric districts\n\t•\tUrban assassinations\n\nAesthetic\n\t•\tOld-world military styling\n\t•\tCapes, long coats, ceremonial markings\n\t•\tStylish and unsettling\n\nReputation\n\n“They kill you politely.”\n","x":-1960,"y":640,"width":410,"height":400},
		{"id":"50b98c2d34c2f0b8","type":"text","text":"1. Black Meridian Group (BMG)\n\nOrigin: Anglo-American\nPublic Cover: Energy infrastructure security & convoy protection\nTrue Function: Offensive security, drone-hunting, counter-insurgency for hire\n\nSpecialty\n\t•\tOil fields, desalination plants, megacity logistics\n\t•\tCounter-drone nets and electronic warfare\n\t•\tRapid escalation response\n\nAesthetic\n\t•\tMatte black armor with desert tan accents\n\t•\tModular exoskeleton braces (non-powered, “assistive”)\n\t•\tLooks like a private army pretending not to be one\n\nReputation\n\n“They don’t start wars. They just make sure they finish.”\n\n⸻\n\n2. Al-Sahra Strategic Services\n\nOrigin: Gulf-state funded (UAE/Saudi shell consortium)\nPublic Cover: Regional stabilization & counter-terrorism training\nTrue Function: Proxy force used to shape succession politics and suppress unrest\n\nSpecialty\n\t•\tUrban pacification\n\t•\tTargeted eliminations\n\t•\tTraining loyalist militias\n\nAesthetic\n\t•\tClean, modern kit with gold or white markings\n\t•\tReligious-neutral but culturally adapted iconography\n\t•\tLooks too professional for a private company\n\nReputation\n\n“If Al-Sahra shows up, someone important already lost.”\n\n⸻\n\n3. Helios Reach Solutions\n\nOrigin: EU / Mediterraneum corporate bloc\nPublic Cover: Border security and humanitarian escort\nTrue Function: Intelligence harvesting and influence mapping\n\nSpecialty\n\t•\tRefugee flow control\n\t•\tSensor grids\n\t•\tNarrative shaping (media + NGOs)\n\nAesthetic\n\t•\tLight armor, white/gray palettes\n\t•\tVisually indistinguishable from UN or NGO security\n\t•\tCameras everywhere\n\nReputation\n\n“They don’t shoot first. They record who should be shot later.”\n\n⸻\n\n4. Iron Covenant\n\nOrigin: Ex-militant networks + Eastern European operators\nPublic Cover: Religious site protection\nTrue Function: Ideological warfare & deniable holy war proxy\n\nSpecialty\n\t•\tShrine security\n\t•\tSectarian proxy fighting\n\t•\tPsychological warfare\n\nAesthetic\n\t•\tHeavy armor, religious symbols etched into plates\n\t•\tBrutalist, medieval-meets-modern look\n\t•\tFeels like crusaders with rifles\n\nReputation\n\n“Faith-backed violence is still violence.”","x":-1950,"y":1080,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"4a2958a0459129c9","type":"text","text":"(Resource extraction, state collapse, proxy empires)\n\n1. Red Horizon Collective\n\nOrigin: Post-Wagner / Africa Corps derivative\nPublic Cover: Counter-terrorism support\nTrue Function: Regime survival and extraction enforcement\n\nSpecialty\n\t•\tRegime protection\n\t•\tMining zones\n\t•\tCounter-insurgency\n\nAesthetic\n\t•\tHeavy, worn gear\n\t•\tSoviet-meets-scrap look\n\t•\tBrutal, utilitarian\n\nReputation\n\n“They stay as long as the money does.”\n\n⸻\n\n2. Obsidian Atlas\n\nOrigin: Pan-African corporate coalition\nPublic Cover: Infrastructure protection\nTrue Function: Resource corridor control\n\nSpecialty\n\t•\tRail lines\n\t•\tDams\n\t•\tRare earth extraction zones\n\nAesthetic\n\t•\tBlack-and-copper armor\n\t•\tIndustrial symbolism\n\t•\tLooks like miners with guns\n\nReputation\n\n“If Obsidian Atlas guards it, it’s worth killing for.”\n\n⸻\n\n3. Zambezi Strategic\n\nOrigin: Southern Africa\nPublic Cover: Wildlife protection\nTrue Function: Land clearance & population displacement\n\nSpecialty\n\t•\tAnti-poaching cover\n\t•\tForced relocations\n\t•\tTerrain denial\n\nAesthetic\n\t•\tGreen camo, animal motifs\n\t•\tHunter aesthetic\n\t•\tEco-violence irony\n\nReputation\n\n“They save animals. People are optional.”\n\n⸻\n\n4. Sunfall Dynamics\n\nOrigin: Chinese-linked\nPublic Cover: Development security\nTrue Function: Long-term influence and surveillance\n\nSpecialty\n\t•\tSmart cities\n\t•\tDigital identity enforcement\n\t•\tLabor control\n\nAesthetic\n\t•\tClean, high-tech\n\t•\tSubtle glowing interfaces\n\t•\tLooks friendly until it isn’t\n\nReputation\n\n“They don’t leave.”\n","x":-1950,"y":200,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"0fa0d82c80c40ff9","type":"text","text":"1. Hǎidōng Integrated Solutions\n\nOrigin: China\nPublic Cover: Border logistics & disaster response\nTrue Function: Evo5/TBS field testing\n\nSpecialty\n\t•\t“Wildlife incidents”\n\t•\tMechanized target suppression\n\t•\tBiological systems integration\n\nAesthetic\n\t•\tWhite-green armor\n\t•\tBio-sensor visors\n\t•\tLooks like medics escorting monsters\n\n⸻\n\n2. Trinetra Defense Group\n\nOrigin: India\nPublic Cover: Infrastructure security\nTrue Function: Counter-biological warfare & deniable retaliation\n\nSpecialty\n\t•\tSensor warfare\n\t•\tHigh-altitude operations\n\t•\tCounter-TBS tactics\n\nAesthetic\n\t•\tDark blue and saffron highlights\n\t•\tAncient symbolism + modern kit\n\t•\tWarrior-philosopher vibe\n\n⸻\n\n3. Iron Lotus Consortium\n\nOrigin: Sino-Indian shell joint venture\nPublic Cover: Peacekeeping force\nTrue Function: Controlled conflict maintenance\n\nSpecialty\n\t•\tFalse-flag engagements\n\t•\tIncident management\n\t•\tMedia manipulation\n\nAesthetic\n\t•\tNeutral gray armor\n\t•\tNo insignia\n\t•\tLooks deliberately bland\n\n⸻\n\n4. Black Channel Group\n\nOrigin: Stateless / elite ex-operators\nPublic Cover: None\nTrue Function: Nobody knows—probably everything illegal\n\nSpecialty\n\t•\tAssassinations\n\t•\tArtifact extraction\n\t•\t“Accidental” escalations\n\nAesthetic\n\t•\tMatte black, featureless\n\t•\tNo voice comms visible\n\t•\tGhosts with rifles\n\nReputation\n\n“If Black Channel was there, the story you heard is a lie.”","x":-1950,"y":-260,"width":400,"height":420}
	],
